I had a couple of deaths to mimics in very early shops.  Since then
I've been more careful about shops in the extremely early game (I
still use them to price-check items I'm carrying, but I don't usually
check the shop's inventory), but here's my question:  approximately
how *long* do I need to wait, to be relatively sure that shop use
won't be fatal?  Mimics aren't particularly dangerous a little later
in the game, but how _much_ later are we talking?  How many hitpoints,
and what level of equipment and/or experience, would adequately
prepare me to take out an early mimic without weakening myself
dangerously?


